BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Petaluma River History Paddle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260621T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260621T120000
UID:8a9ef13436a8694b298398929f3ac2c9@thefloathousepetaluma.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/63
 02d39abd02437a9e9f0276/1769554819341-GSKOMFLWE47GHOKQMBJW/Petaluma+River+H
 istory+Paddle+2026+for+squarespace+calendar+%281500+x+1000+px%29.png
DESCRIPTION:Petaluma River History Paddle The Petaluma River is the reason
  there’s a city here. Long before highways and railroads\, this tidal wa
 terway was the region’s saltwater highway —a working river that powere
 d Petaluma’s rise and connected Sonoma County’s farms and businesses t
 o San Francisco\, the Gold Rush\, and markets around the world. On this tw
 o-hour\, gentle guided paddle \, history comes alive through storytelling 
 from multiple points of view. You’ll paddle in stable sit-on-top kayaks 
 with an experienced\, costumed guide\, while costumed actors on shore step
  into the lives of real Petalumans who once depended on the river for thei
 r livelihood. Hear stories from people who worked the egg trade\, ran mess
 ages between businesses\, managed boarding houses\, and built enterprises 
 that fueled a growing city. As you move through downtown and along histori
 c riverbanks\, you’ll gain a deeper appreciation for the ingenuity\, ind
 ustrious spirit\, and daily lives that shaped Petaluma—and the river tha
 t made it all possible. No paddling experience necessary. All equipment an
 d instruction provided. Just bring your curiosity—and be ready to see Pe
 taluma through new eyes. $75/person. Includes everything\, even insight! R
 eserve your spot here! #block-186fb3210b9d4444859c { --tweak-text-block-ra
 dius: 0px 0px 0px 0px\; --tweak-text-block-radius: unset\; --stroke-style:
  none\;--stroke-thickness: 6px\; --tweak-text-block-background-color: init
 ial\; } #block-186fb3210b9d4444859c .sqs-html-content { --tweak-text-block
 -padding: 6% 6% 6% 6%\; --tweak-text-block-padding: initial\; } #block-186
 fb3210b9d4444859c { mix-blend-mode: var(--tweak-text-block-blend )\; } #bl
 ock-186fb3210b9d4444859c { } @media screen and (max-width: 767px) { #block
 -186fb3210b9d4444859c { } } @media screen and (max-width: 767px) { #block-
 186fb3210b9d4444859c .sqs-html-content { } } @media screen and (max-width:
  767px) { }
LOCATION:The Floathouse Petaluma\, 50 Water Street\, Petaluma\, CA\, 94952
URL:https://www.thefloathousepetaluma.org/events/petaluma-river-history-pa
 ddle-june-21-2026
X-SOURCE:The Floathouse Petaluma
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Learn to SUP: Build skills. Find flow. Love the river. 
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260628T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260628T110000
UID:29f65f0f4ed96644f6aacb15cbc9b1ba@thefloathousepetaluma.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/63
 02d39abd02437a9e9f0276/1771550281507-265ECDHT7D3N331PAKVN/Learn+to+SUP+wit
 h+us++2026+Squarespace+image+%281500+x+1000+px%29.png
DESCRIPTION:Learn to SUP: Build Skills. Find Flow. Ready to feel confident
  on a paddleboard? Our Learn to SUP class is a welcoming\, two-hour introd
 uction designed to help you paddle smarter — not harder — so you can t
 ruly enjoy your time on the water. Start your SUP journey here. For just $
 60 \, you’ll learn from an ACA-certified (American Canoe Association) in
 structor in a small\, supportive group of just 2–6 students . That means
  personalized attention\, real feedback\, and space to grow. We’ll cover
 : Proper stance and balance Efficient paddle technique Turning and maneuve
 ring Launching and returning to the dock River awareness and safety basics
  Many people hop on a board and think they’re having fun — but they’
 re working twice as hard as they need to. This class unlocks the “aha”
  moments that make paddleboarding smoother\, more efficient\, and way more
  enjoyable. Held right in the heart of downtown Petaluma on the beautiful 
 Petaluma River\, this is your chance to build skills in a calm\, supportiv
 e environment — and start feeling at home on the water. Bring a friend\,
  learn together\, and find your flow. All equipment included. Only 6 paddl
 ers per class. Book your spot early. #block-a8f0867bd77e22974018 { --tweak
 -text-block-radius: 0px 0px 0px 0px\; --tweak-text-block-radius: unset\; -
 -stroke-style: none\;--stroke-thickness: 6px\; --tweak-text-block-backgrou
